nL45: \nL46: ## Information For\nL47: \nL48:   * 【33†Consumers】\nL49:   * 【34†Patients】\nL50:   * 【35†Industry】\nL51:   * 【36†Health Professionals】\nL52:   * 【37†Federal, State and Local Officials】\nL53: \nL54: FDA News Release\nL55: # FDA Approves First Drug to Treat Alexander Disease\nL56: \nL57: New therapy is the first to directly target the underlying cause of this rare neurological disease\nL58: \nL59: For Immediate Release:\nL60:     September 03, 2026\nL61: The U.S. Food and Drug Administration has approved Zanvastro (zilganersen) injection for the treatment of Alexander disease in pediatric and adult patients. Zanvastro is the first FDA-approved treatment for Alexander disease and the first therapy to directly target the protein buildup that drives the disease.\nL62: “For patients with Alexander disease and their families, there have been no approved treatment options — only supportive care while the disease progresses,” said Emily Freilich, M.D., Director of the Division of Neurology I in the FDA’s Center for Drug Evaluation and Research. “Today’s approval is a landmark moment for this community, offering the first therapy that addresses the underlying cause of this rare and serious disease.”\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFDA approves treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis associated with a mutation in the SOD1 gene | FDA (https://www.fda.gov/drugs/news-events-human-drugs/fda-approves-treatment-amyotrophic-lateral-sclerosis-associated-mutation-sod1-gene)\nciteturn98view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.fda.gov/drugs/news-events-human-drugs/fda-approves-treatment-amyotrophic-lateral-sclerosis-associated-mutation-sod1-gene\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 106\nL0:   * 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1:   * 【1†Skip to FDA Search】\nL2:   * 【2†Skip to in this section menu】\nL3:   * 【3†Skip to footer links】\nL4: \nL5: 【4†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL6: \nL7:   *   Search\nL8:   *   Menu\nL9: \nL10: Search FDA [Input: Search FDA] Submit search\nL11: \nL12: ## Featured\nL13: \nL14:   * 【5†Report a Product Problem†contact.fda.gov】\nL15:   * 【6†Contact FDA】\nL16:   * 【7†FDA Guidance Documents】\nL17:   * 【8†Recalls, Market Withdrawals and Safety Alerts】\nL18:   * 【9†Press Announcements】\nL19:   * 【10†Warning Letters】\nL20:   * 【11†Advisory Committees】\nL21:   * 【12†En Español】\nL22: ## Products\nL23: \nL24:   * 【13†Food】\nL25:   * 【14†Drugs】\nL26:   * 【15†Medical Devices】\nL27:   * 【16†Radiation-Emitting Products】\nL28:   * 【17†Vaccines, Blood, and Biologics】\nL29:   * 【18†Animal and Veterinary】\nL30:   * 【19†Cosmetics】\nL31:   * 【20†Tobacco Products】\nL32: ## Topics\nL33: \nL34:   * 【21†About FDA】\nL35:   * 【22†Combination Products】\nL36:   * 【23†Regulatory Information】\nL37:   * 【24†Safety】\nL38:   * 【25†Emergency Preparedness】\nL39:   * 【26†International Programs】\nL40:   * 【27†News and Events】\nL41:   * 【28†Training and Continuing Education】\nL42:   * 【29†Inspections and Compliance】\nL43:   * 【30†Science and Research】\nL44: ## Information For\nL45: \nL46:   * 【31†Consumers】\nL47:   * 【32†Patients】\nL48:   * 【33†Industry】\nL49:   * 【34†Health Professionals】\nL50:   * 【35†Federal, State and Local Officials】\nL51: \nL52:   * 【36†News & Events for Human Drugs】\nL53: \nL54:     * 【37†Meetings, Conferences, & Workshops | Drugs】\nL55:     * 【38†Notable Approvals | Drugs】\nL56: \nL57:     * 【39†CDER Conversations】\nL58:     * 【40†From Our Perspective】\nL59:     * 【41†Spotlight on CDER Science】\nL60:     * 【42†Things to Know About...】\nL61: # FDA approves treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis associated with a mutation in the SOD1 gene\nL62: ## Action\nL63: \nL64: FDA approved Qalsody (tofersen) to treat patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) associated with a mutation in the superoxide dismutase 1 (SOD1) gene (SOD1-ALS). Qalsody is an antisense oligonucleotide that targets SOD1 mRNA to reduce the synthesis of SOD1 protein. The approval was based on a reduction in plasma neurofilament light (NfL), a blood-based biomarker of axonal (nerve) injury and neurodegeneration.\nL65: Qalsody is administered intrathecally (through a spinal injection) by healthcare professionals who are experienced in performing lumbar punctures. The recommended dosage is 100 mg (15 mL) per administration. Patients receive three initial doses administered at 14-day intervals, followed by a maintenance dose every 28 days.\nL66: ### Disease or Condition\nL67: \nL68: Similar to sporadic 【43†ALS†www.ninds.nih.gov】, where there are no associated risk factors and no family history of the disease, SOD1-ALS is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that attacks and kills the nerve cells that control voluntary muscles. Voluntary muscles produce movements such as chewing, walking, breathing, and talking. ALS causes the nerves to lose the ability to activate specific muscles, which causes the muscles to become weak and leads to paralysis.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCAMP4 Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Corporate Highlights • Thu, 11/05/2026 - 16:05 (https://investors.camp4tx.com/news-releases/news-release-details/camp4-reports-third-quarter-2026-financial-results-and-corporate)\nciteturn98view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://investors.camp4tx.com/news-releases/news-release-details/camp4-reports-third-quarter-2026-financial-results-and-corporate\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: Menu Close\nL1: \nL2: Follow\nL3: \nL4: RNA therapeutics that aim to restore healthy protein levels\nL5:   * 【0†Science†www.camp4tx.com】\nL6:     * 【1†regRNA†www.camp4tx.com】\nL7:     * 【2†RAP Platform®†www.camp4tx.com】\nL8:     * 【3†Publications†www.camp4tx.com】\nL9:   * 【4†About†www.camp4tx.com】\nL10:     * 【5†Leadership Team†www.camp4tx.com】\nL11:     * 【6†Join CAMP4†www.camp4tx.com】\nL12:     * 【7†Mission & Vision†www.camp4tx.com】\nL13:     * 【8†Virtues†www.camp4tx.com】\nL14:   * 【9†Pipeline†www.camp4tx.com】\nL15:     * 【10†Partnerships†www.camp4tx.com】\nL16:   * 【11†Investors】\nL17:   * 【12†Disease Areas†www.camp4tx.com】\nL18:   * 【13†Contact†www.camp4tx.com】\nL19: 【14†Image†www.camp4tx.com】\nL20: # Release Details\nL21: \nL22: Investor Menu\nL23:   * 【15†Overview】\nL24:   * 【16†News & Events】\nL25:     * 【16†News Releases】\nL26:     * 【17†Events】\nL27:     * 【18†Presentations】\nL28:   * 【19†Stock】\nL29:     * 【19†Stock Quote & Chart】\nL30:     * 【20†Analyst Coverage】\nL31:   * 【21†Governance】\nL32:     * 【21†Documents & Charters】\nL33:     * 【22†Board of Directors†www.camp4tx.com】\nL34:     * 【23†Management†www.camp4tx.com】\nL35:     * 【24†Committee Composition】\nL36:   * 【25†Financials】\nL37:     * 【25†SEC Filings】\nL38:   * 【26†Resources】\nL39:     * 【26†Investor FAQs】\nL40:     * 【27†Email Alerts】\nL41:     * 【28†Contact Us】\nL42: ##\nL43: \nL44: CAMP4 Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Corporate Highlights\nL45: \nL46: November 5, 2026\nL47: \nL48: 【29†PDF Version】\nL49: \nL50: Received authorization in the United Kingdom and European Union to expand global first-in-human ASCEND Phase 1/2 clinical trial of CMP-002 in patients with SYNGAP1-related disorder, adding to clearances in Australia and Argentina\nL51: \nL52: Company remains on track to dose first patient by year-end 2026\nL53: Hosted Virtual Analyst Day highlighting the unmet need in SYNGAP1-related disorder and the design of the ASCEND Phase 1/2 clinical; announced SHANK3 for Phelan-McDermid syndrome as next pipeline program\nL54: \nL55: Received $50.1 million from second closing of private placement; cash and cash equivalents of $124.5 million as of September 30, 2026, with cash runway expected through the end of 2028\nL56: WATERTOWN, Mass., Nov.\nL57: 05, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- 【30†CAMP4 Therapeutics Corporation†www.globenewswire.com】 (“CAMP4” or “the Company”) (Nasdaq: CAMP), a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing a pipeline of regulatory RNA-targeting therapeutics designed to upregulate gene expression with the goal of restoring healthy protein levels to treat a broad range of genetic diseases, today announced financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026, and provided recent corporate highlights.\nL58: “The third quarter was one of continued execution for CAMP4. With regulatory clearances now in place in Australia, Argentina, the United Kingdom, and the European Union, we have launched our first-in-human ASCEND Phase 1/2 clinical trial of CMP-002 in patients with SYNGAP1-related disorder,” said Josh Mandel-Brehm, President and Chief Executive Officer of CAMP4.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://go.bio.org/rs/490-EHZ-999/images/ClinicalDevelopmentSuccessRates2011_2020.pdf)\nciteturn98view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 34; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://go.bio.org/rs/490-EHZ-999/images/ClinicalDevelopmentSuccessRates2011_2020.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1440\nL0@P0: Clinical Development\nL1@P0: Success Rates and\nL2@P0: Contributing Factors\nL3@P0-1: 2011–20202/ February 2021 © BIO | QLS Advisors | Informa UK Ltd 2021 (Unauthorized photocopying prohibited.)\nL4@P1: About BIO\nL5@P1: BIO is the world’s largest trade association representing biotechnology companies, academic institutions, state\nL6@P1: biotechnology centers, and related organizations across the United States and in more than 30 other nations.\nL7@P1: BIO members, from the entrepreneurial to the Fortune 500 multinationals, are involved in the research and\nL8@P1: development of innovative healthcare, agricultural, industrial, and environmental biotechnology products.\nL9@P1: BIO also produces industry-leading investor and partnering events to strengthen the innovator ecosystem.\nL10@P1: About Informa Pharma Intelligence\nL11@P1: Biomedtracker, a subscription-based product of Informa Pharma Intelligence, tracks the clinical development\nL12@P1: and regulatory history of investigational drugs to assess their Likelihood of Approval (LOA) by the FDA.\nL13@P1: Biomedtracker is populated in near real-time with updated information from press releases, corporate\nL14@P1: earnings calls, investor and medical meetings, and numerous other sources. These data can be visualized,\nL15@P1: analyzed, and interpreted in the specifically designed R&D benchmarking tool Pharmapremia. This provides\nL16@P1: an exclusive window into drug development pipelines and paints a fuller, clearer picture of how the industry\nL17@P1: is performing. For more information visit www.pharmaintelligence.informa.com.\nL18@P1: About QLS Advisors\nL19@P1: QLS Advisors LLC is a technology and advisory company based in Cambridge, MA, dedicated to fostering\nL20@P1: innovation in the life sciences. QLS employs a unique blend of fundamental and quantitative tools to help\nL21@P1: clients manage risk, assess reward, and develop investment and financing strategies for portfolios of\nL22@P1-2: healthcare-related assets. For more information visit www.qlsadvisors.com.3/ February 2021 © BIO | QLS Advisors | Informa UK Ltd 2021 (Unauthorized photocopying prohibited.)\nL23@P2: Executive Summary\nL24@P2: This is both an updated study of clinical drug development success rates from our 2016 report, and an\nL25@P2: expansion into the drivers of success with the addition of machine learning modeling to analyze the predictive\nL26@P2: factors contributing to drug development. A total of 12,728 clinical and regulatory phase transitions were\nL27@P2: recorded and analyzed from 9,704 development programs over the last decade (2011–2020), across 1,779\nL28@P2: companies in the Biomedtracker database. Phase transitions occur when a drug candidate advances into\n"
